 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Petrol is about **13.5% dearer** than a year ago. In August 2026 the automotive fuel price index was 112.95, against 99.49 in August 2025.\n\nThe price has been volatile over the past year:\n\n- **Early 2026:** prices fell, with January down 2.7% and February down 7.2% year on year.\n- **March 2026:** a sharp spike, up 24.2% year on year, with April up 18.6%.\n- **June 2026:** prices dropped back, down 7.3% year on year.\n- **August 2026:** prices jumped again, up 13.5% year on year and 15% higher than June's low.\n\nThe ABS publishes this as an index rather than a cents-per-litre price, so I can't give you an exact dollar figure per litre. The 13.5% is the average across Australia's capital cities, and your local station may differ.",
